<title>USA: NYS plans to sell $215 mln of bonds competitively.</title>
<headline>NYS plans to sell $215 mln of bonds competitively.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York State on Tuesday said that it plans to sell on March 12 approximately $215.42 million of general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>Bruce Balle, director of debt management for New York State, said that the offering will be through competitive auction.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
